<content><![CDATA[<oer-draft note="Brief from the DART 413 course plan. Revise it, then Publish to show it to readers.">
<p>Design a 2.5D relief tile from a heightmap or modeled surface, set up the CAM job, and have it cut. Fallback if CNC time is unavailable: laser-cut stacked contours of the same surface.</p>
<h2>What to hand in</h2>
<ul><li>The tile</li><li>CAM setup screenshots with bit/feeds/speeds justified</li></ul>
<h2>What you'll practise</h2>
<ul><li>Set up a CAM job</li><li>Think in 2.5D</li></ul>
<p>Time: 2 weeks (tech-run)</p>
</oer-draft>
